ue":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"427"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T07:13:42-07:00","id":1152795,"title":"","content":"Vagina dentata would probably be thematically appropriate (the so-called &quot;Terrible Mother&quot; archetype from Jung that shows up in certain Hindu, Shinto, Maori and other myths) but too far outside of most players' comfort zones, me suspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:08:52-07:00","id":1155452,"title":"","content":"How about somebody who's feet are warped into a backwards curly shape, just like those funny shoes that jesters are known to wear?<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.harr-shoes.com/data/media/9/908_200x300_spezial__li.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T14:41:27-07:00","id":1155544,"title":"","content":"I have no mouth (and I must scream)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:54:34-07:00","id":1155603,"title":"","content":"A Knocker who's tongue is double the length of a normal human's, causing them to develop a chronic speech impediment as they struggle to keep it in their mouths.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Pooka who is unable to fully conceal the presence of their tail from mortals, leading them to believe they have some sort of atavistic 5th limb.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Satyr for whom even the greatest of worldly pleasures quickly grow stale, leaving them with a gnawing sense of unfilfillment as they struggle to find excitement in their lives.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Troll who suffers from anti social personality disorder, and thus finds their duty of protecting others to be a source of great irritation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T15:37:48-08:00","id":1169500,"title":"","content":"How about a sluagh who sounds like children screaming every time they talk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T17:21:55-08:00","id":1169532,"title":"","content":"A Sidhe with a deformed spine similar to Richard III.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T08:11:22-08:00","id":1169636,"title":"","content":"A Satyr who suffers from a persistent case of erectile dysfunction, leaving him irritable and aggressive.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Redcap who's teeth resemble those of a normal human, requiring greater effort to properly chew tough materials.<br /> <br /> <br /> A reptilian Pooka who's developed a forked tongue, resulting in them having a lisp when they speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Knocker who has to rely on crutches to move around. In their true form, their body's proportions are screwed up, resulting in lengthy arms and short legs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T12:21:13-08:00","id":1171848,"title":"","content":"Try this idea deformities of the mind. The prankster who aways goes to far. The eternally laughing maiden whose eyes are cold and bitter. The knight who seems always ready to fly into a rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T12:23:34-08:00","id":1171850,"title":"","content":"Try this physical trait. Infestation. The beautiful sidhe crawling with bugs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T19:13:46-08:00","id":1186517,"title":"","content":"A Sidhe Lord with six additional eyes that form a 5 pointed star around the forehead. All six eyes seem to act independently of one another, even blinking out of sequence.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Knocker Squire with an oversize cranium that pulses with bulging veins. When asked about it, they smirk and claim that their head is <i>'bursting with new ideas.'</i><br /> <br /> <br /> A Boggan Squire with a third hand where their right foot should be. They claim to be able to carry out three tasks at the same time while standing on one leg.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Troll Knight who violently refuses to go outside during the day, claiming some nonsense about <i>'turning to stone'</i> under the sun's rays.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Satyr Baron who's chimerical head is replaced with that of a goat's. They communicate in broken, disjointed sentences due to the complications involving their vocal components.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-15T23:42:13-08:00","id":1186555,"title":"","content":"Inspired by Madame Medusa from Marvel Comics, a sidhe woman who's hair twitchs and writhes. This is very subtle in her mortal seeming and dramatic in fae from. She has figured out certain cantrips that let her use her hair like Madame Medusa at the cost of glamor. So while it's still a deformity she cam surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T10:29:06-08:00","id":1187072,"title":"","content":"<b>Sidhe Lord</b> with a vertical third eye that, when fully opened, takes up 20% of their forehead's surface. The tear duct is located directly above the bridge of their nose.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sluagh Knight</b> who has no eye sockets and instead navigates their surroundings through heightened senses of sound, smell, taste and touch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Redcap Knight</b> with an unhinging jaw, opening their mouth to disgusting proportions as they prepare to take a bite out of something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pooka Squire</b> who has a blow hole on the back of their neck. They claim it saves them the trouble of having to buy a snorkel when they go swimming.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Eshu Baron</b> who is clinically deaf; they can still tell amazing stories, but can't hear them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Troll Lord</b> with a chimerical second head who provides commentary and advice derived from their alternate Legacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Satyr Baron</b> who has an extra pair of inverted horn growing up from the back of their cranium and over towards the front. Together, the two sets of horns vaguely resemble a crown of nobility.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Selkie Baron</b> with a pair of enlarged tusks, their appearance bares a closer resemblance to that of a bloated walrus than a playful seal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Piskie Squire</b> who is missing their right hand, claiming it was amputated long ago as punishment for stealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-01-2018, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:29:43-07:00","id":1202022,"title":"","content":"A water deer Pooka, who's prominent fangs often cause strangers to confuse them for being a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T12:33:07-07:00","id":1203103,"title":"","content":"I guess a Satyr of House Balor with the same problem as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Priapus\" target=\"_blank\">Priapus</a> would be kind of tacky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}